# Git commits (Dose)

Commit when the user asks, or when they said commits as you go.

## Safety

- NEVER update git config.
- NEVER skip hooks (`--no-verify`). If a hook fails, fix and make a **new** commit.
- NEVER commit `.env`, credentials, or `node_modules`.
- Avoid `--amend` unless the user asked, HEAD is yours this session, and it is unpushed.

## When committing

Run in parallel: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5`.

Stage only relevant files. Message format (commitlint `type(scope): subject`, subject not sentence-case):

```sh
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat(notes): filter notes by search query

- Pass q from the search box into Prisma contains filters
EOF
)"
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `config`, `ci`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `style`, `build`. Body bullets, line length ≤ 100. Do not push unless asked.
